        "message": "docs: refresh README with verified content, structure, and examples\n\n- Rewrites the README onto the standard Aspose FOSS presentation template:\n  badge row + banner, a Navigation TOC, an At-a-Glance capability diagram,\n  Key Capabilities, Installation, a dedicated Dependencies section, Quick\n  Start, and Additional Examples.\n- Adds a real Dependencies section documenting that the library has no\n  third-party package dependencies of its own, plus the real native/system\n  toolchain requirements (CMake, a C++17 compiler, Ninja).\n- Adds a module-grouped API Reference table plus curated core/internal\n  classes, collapsed behind a <details> disclosure so the page stays\n  scannable.\n- Adds a Documentation & Resources section linking the real getting-started\n  guide, how-to/FAQ articles, full API reference, and the issue tracker.\n- Adds a Scope and Limitations section naming the real, verified constraints\n  of this FOSS build, closed by a single standalone paragraph pointing to\n  the Enterprise Edition for broader functionality.\n- Adds Development and Testing instructions and a standard MIT License\n  section linking the real license file.\n\nVerification: every code example and dependency claim was checked against\nthe real, current package surface; every claim in Scope and Limitations was\nverified against source; the diagram and API Reference detail were checked\nwith this project's own automated structural/content gates before this\nchange was proposed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
